<!-- ============================================================
       FAQs
  ============================================================ -->
  <section class="sec sec-canvas">
    <div class="container">

      <div class="row">
        <div class="col-12">
          <span class="zin-eyebrow">FAQs</span>
          <h2 class="zin-h2">The questions people ask.</h2>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="row">
        <div class="col-md-8">

          <div class="accordion" id="zinFaq">

            <div class="faq-item">
              <button class="faq-btn" data-bs-toggle="collapse" data-bs-target="#faq1" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="faq1">
                Can't I just use Notion or Apple Notes?
                <span class="faq-chevron" aria-hidden="true">▾</span>
              </button>
              <div id="faq1" class="collapse" data-bs-parent="#zinFaq">
                <p class="faq-answer">You can. But general tools weren't built for this job. No mining prompt. No reading mode. No prompt assembly. Most people don't maintain them consistently enough to produce content from them.</p>
              </div>
            </div>

            <div class="faq-item">
              <button class="faq-btn" data-bs-toggle="collapse" data-bs-target="#faq2" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="faq2">
                Won't AI just do this anyway?
                <span class="faq-chevron" aria-hidden="true">▾</span>
              </button>
              <div id="faq2" class="collapse" data-bs-parent="#zinFaq">
                <p class="faq-answer">AI can't invent your client stories, your real observations, or the phrase only you would say. Zin captures those. That's what makes the AI output stop being generic.</p>
              </div>
            </div>

            <div class="faq-item">
              <button class="faq-btn" data-bs-toggle="collapse" data-bs-target="#faq3" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="faq3">
                Is this another system I'll abandon?
                <span class="faq-chevron" aria-hidden="true">▾</span>
              </button>
              <div id="faq3" class="collapse" data-bs-parent="#zinFaq">
                <p class="faq-answer">Zin is designed to be minimal. Capture takes seconds. There's no maintenance. It gets more useful the longer you use it, without becoming a project in itself.</p>
              </div>
            </div>

            <div class="faq-item">
              <button class="faq-btn" data-bs-toggle="collapse" data-bs-target="#faq4" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="faq4">
                Do I have time for this?
                <span class="faq-chevron" aria-hidden="true">▾</span>
              </button>
              <div id="faq4" class="collapse" data-bs-parent="#zinFaq">
                <p class="faq-answer">The bootstrap takes one session. Daily capture is two to five minutes. You save that time back the moment you sit down to write.</p>
              </div>
            </div>

          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>